# Use the audio-curation agent for audio tasks

For ANY task involving audio files or audio datasets — e.g. file durations, quality
filtering, VAD/segmentation, resampling / mono conversion, transcription (ASR), WER,
diarization, building a TTS/ASR training set, or exporting an audio manifest — drive the
`nemo_curator.audio_agent` tool core. **Do NOT write ad-hoc shell/Python** (ffprobe,
soundfile, librosa, torchaudio loops) to inspect or process the audio, even for a
"quick" one-off like reading durations — use `GetAudioDurationStage` via the agent.

Follow the workflow in
[audio-agent.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/audio-agent.mdc) and
[SKILL.md](mdc:.claude/skills/audio-curation/SKILL.md): route → `validate` → `smoke` →
confirm → `run` → `report`, using only real stages from `discover` / `cards` / `describe`
(never invent names) and honoring the confirm gate (no silent full-scale runs).

Run verbs with the repo virtualenv from the repo root:
`.venv/bin/python -m nemo_curator.audio_agent <verb> [args]`.
